#: src/telephony/ui/windows/settings_window.py:311
msgid ""
"The Default Country Code is used to format numbers that don't include an "
"international prefix (e.g., +358).\n"
"\n"
"If left empty, the system tries to detect it automatically from your SIM "
"card or network.\n"
"\n"
"You can manually override it here by entering a 2-letter ISO region code (e."
"g. US, FI, DE) or a calling code (e.g. +358, 358, +1, 1)."
msgstr ""
"Ti Default a Kodigo ti Pagilian ket maus-usar a mangpormat kadagiti numero a "
"saan a mangiraman ti internasional a pangrugian (e.g., +358).\n"
"\n"
"No mabaybay-an nga awan ti kargana, automatiko nga ikagumaan ti sistema a "
"detektaren dayta manipud iti SIM card wenno network-mo.\n"
"\n"
"Mabalinmo a manual a baliwan daytoy ditoy babaen ti panangikabil ti 2-letra "
"a kodigo ti rehion ti ISO (e.g. US, FI, DE) wenno ti kodigo ti panagayab (e."
"g. +358, 358, +1, 1)."

#: src/telephony/ui/windows/settings_window.py:332
msgid ""
"The ringback tone is the sound played (toot-toot-toot) while waiting for an "
"outgoing call to be answered. Some carriers don't generate it so we have "
"option to generate it manually here. \n"
"\n"
"You can select your own music file, or clear it to use the standard system "
"tone."
msgstr ""
"Ti ringback tone ket ti uni a maipatokar (toot-toot-toot) bayat ti panagur-"
"uray a masungbatan ti rumrummuar nga awag. Dadduma a carrier ket saan a "
"mangpataud iti dayta isu nga adda pagpiliantayo a mangpataud iti manual "
"ditoy. \n"
"\n"
"Mabalinmo ti agpili ti bukodmo a musika a file, wenno ikkaten daytoy tapno "
"mausar ti gagangay a tono ti sistema."

#: src/telephony/ui/windows/settings_window.py:352
msgid "Select Ringback Tone"
msgstr "Pilien ti Ringback Tone"

#: src/telephony/ui/windows/settings_window.py:360
msgid "Audio Files"
